<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Al-Mansur Abdallah ibn Hamza</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1166–<a href="/years/1217">1217</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/12th-century">12th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Al-Mansur Abdallah ibn Hamza was Zaydi <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/imam">imam</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yemen">Yemen</a> from 1187 to 1217 and one of the most prolific Zaydi scholars. He revived the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/imamate">imamate</a> in the northern highlands and fought the Ayyubid rulers of Yemen. He also harshly suppressed the Mutarrifiyya, a dissident Zaydi sect, and his many writings shaped later Zaydi doctrine.</p></div>
